      {
        "id": 67555,
        "name": "ketigid",
        "username": "ketigid",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/9fc29f/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-07-12T02:25:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"TheJayMann\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/48/2261_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TheJayMann:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I like the idea that if you manage to destroy a card which is currently responding to it's own destruction, it gets fully destroyed with no further reaction and the current one is canceled.&nbsp; Thus if wagons are destroyed, they first start to deal damage.&nbsp; If they destroy a Bee Bot this way, and Unity uses this to destroy the wagons, then the wagons are destroyed with no self reaction, and any damage it had not yet dealt would be cancelled.I'm not trying to say this is the way it works, just that I like the idea.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I like this too. Unique shenanigans makes Sentinels fun!</p>",
        "post_number": 28,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:45:36.014Z",
